The compilation environment doesn't have `ap_int.h` available as a standalone include. Since `ap_int.h` is typically available in Vitis HLS synthesis but not in the plain C++ compilation check, I need to revert to the original function signature (using `char*` and `int*`) and implement coalescing using standard `memcpy` with burst-friendly access patterns instead of the wide bus type approach. The key coalescing benefits (burst transfers, partitioning) are retained through pragma annotations.

